{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1389602-finding-specific-bastions","id":1389602,"title":"Finding specific Bastions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-18T02:44:21-07:00","id":1389602,"title":"Finding specific Bastions","content":"Hello,<br /> I think that in a Changeling session players very often wants to enter a specific person Bastion.<br /> I know that a contract exists to touch a sleeping person and enter his dreams, but how can someone do it in a more traditional way?<br /> Both Gates, ivory and horn, allow you to reach the dreaming roads, but once you got there?<br /> Hedgespinning list in the examples of paradigm shift an option to find the direction for a specific bastion, but hedgespinning doesn t work in the dreaming roads!<br /> Is the only option the Pathfinder contract? Does it work in the dreaming roads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T08:02:19-07:00","id":1389670,"title":"","content":"I would say that, outside extenuating circumstances, you should call for Hedge navigation rolls to find a specific Bastion. According to page 220: &quot;All Dreaming roads are trods with ratings between 3 and 5, and characters navigate them as normal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:09:35-07:00","id":1389721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1389602-finding-specific-bastions?p=1389670#post1389670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that, outside extenuating circumstances, you should call for Hedge navigation rolls to find a specific Bastion. According to page 220: &amp;quot;All Dreaming roads are trods with ratings between 3 and 5, and characters navigate them as normal.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you can use normal navigation if you know, at least vaguely, where is the place you are searching for.<br /> Else i would see no use for the pathfinder contract","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}